{
  "reportDate": "2026-11-13",
  "scope": "Certified cold single-entry writes with bounded browsing and explicit full-preparation fallbacks",
  "methodology": [
    "Release arm64 production store/archive/engine commands in a signed private native validation host; synthetic state only, no real clicks or installed Dev application/data access.",
    "Cold means fresh application/archive/engine caches. Eligible seeds already contain a durable full-validation certificate recorded by their untimed validated creation. The OS disk cache is not purged.",
    "Each size uses one closed seed copied separately for each trial and cold command. The earlier baseline uses equivalent counts, graph/review shape and operation order, not byte-identical database files.",
    "Setup, repository construction/index installation, fixture copying, assertions and frame painting are outside timers. Store command time includes result admission and scheduling page invalidation, not completion of subsequent page rendering.",
    "Missing-proof favorite deletes only the derived certificate before its timer. Enrolled-sense removal keeps its review consumers; both assert complete fallback. No full-load warm-up is hidden in those windows.",
    "The common eight windows retain their preceding stage command boundaries. The harness adds four cold cases and checks explicit partial receipts instead of expecting a whole loaded corpus after eligible writes.",
    "Three trials per size/operation, 72 unique samples; median/min/max are observations, not percentile estimates. The earlier 43-operation inventory was not rerun.",
    "Each fixture has two senses and four examples per entry, semantic/classification records, review enrollments and 1000 retained ratings. It has no image-heavy bodies or dense merged-alias workload. Focused tests cover those safety boundaries, not their large-library latency.",
    "Summary row work counts describe returned scalar rows, not all SQL rows scanned; selected-detail work counts describe payload rows decoded.",
    "Visible-entry counters belong to the primary paged browse model. Separate assertions check auxiliary cold fixture contents and retained review history."
  ],
